    {
      "executionState" : "enabled",
      "id" : "note",
      "kind" : "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters" : {
        "text" : "# Jellyloop Lagoon · Generated textures\nA lasso-drawing arcade game in a goofy cartoon seabed town. Bixby the seahorse fills jelly orders for the Soggy Bun, a scallop-shell diner in Fizzwater Flats, between pear, pebble and lemon houses. On each Run, one fixed-seed FLUX.2 Klein 4B Distilled job paints the 1024 × 1024 lagoon backdrop, and five fixed-seed SDXS 512 jobs generate the seabed sand, the jelly skin, the fruit-house peel, the pastel pebbles and the striped diner shell. Asset Cache stores the six images as named slots for this run and previews each one as it becomes ready. The game starts after all six are ready; later frames reuse the bundle without running either model again. Cancel and Run starts a fresh cache and regenerates all six. Both model packages remain link-only; link the Klein node to the same 4B Distilled package as the bundled Klein example.\n\n**Controls.** Drag in the Trackpad, or drag on the full-screen preview, to swim: Bixby's bubble wand follows the pointer and leaves a trail of soap bubbles. Press Action or Space to start, to toot the bubble horn during a shift (it pushes nearby Grumbles away and stuns them; three toots per shift), and to continue from a result screen.\n\n**Goal.** Draw loops around jellyfish. When your trail crosses itself, or the wand touches an older bubble (the glowing ring), every jelly inside the loop is caught; several jellies in one loop multiply their points. Fill each shift's order (pink, blue and lime counts in the top bar) before the clock runs out. Golden jellies are shy, score extra and add five seconds. Grumbles, the spiky pufferfish, pop any trail they touch and cost a heart when they bump Bixby or end up inside your loop. Serve all four shifts to win. Running out of time or hearts lets you retry the shift with full hearts.\n\n**Settings.** The Game settings JSON sets `shiftTimeScale` (0.5–3), `startingHearts` (1–9), `tootsPerShift` (0–9) and `firstShift` (1–4). Changing a setting restarts the run."
      },
      "resources" : {

      },
      "title" : "How to play"
    },
